.TH VIBEOS-DICTATE 1 "2026-11-16" "vibeos 0.1.0" "VibeOS"
.SH NAME
vibeos-dictate \- dictation for VibeOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibeos-dictate
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turns speech into text on the phone: the microphone button starts and stops listening, and what is said goes at the
end of the document as it is said. Speech is recognised on the phone itself, from the user's default audio source:
English, German and Spanish by Moonshine's streaming transcriber, with punctuation and capitals; French, Italian and
Russian by Vosk, in lower case and without punctuation.
.PP
The language is the app bar's button, which shows its code; it lists the languages whose models are installed. The
choice is kept in the GSettings key
.B vibeos.Dictate language
(empty: the first of the user's languages with a model, else English). Choosing another while listening finishes what
was said, then listens on in the new language.
.PP
The document is not typed in, and no keyboard comes up for it. A long press or a double tap selects a word, and a
drag on from it selects more; a bar over the selection copies it or selects everything.
.PP
The document is kept in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/vibeos-dictate/document.txt .
The application's
.B dictate
action (org.gtk.Actions on /vibeos/Dictate) starts and stops listening as the button does.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/vibeos-dictate/libmoonshine.so, /usr/lib/vibeos-dictate/libvosk.so
The recognisers' libraries, loaded when listening starts (from the system's library path if they are not there).
.TP
.I /usr/share/vibeos-dictate/models/
The models, a directory each, named as their recogniser names them: Moonshine's tiny-streaming-en,
small-streaming-de, ...; Vosk's vosk-model-small-ru-0.22 or vosk-small-ru. The part of the name that is a language's
code is its language. One in
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/vibeos-dictate/models/
is found first. Of several for a language, Moonshine's smallest streaming model is used, then Vosk's.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MOONSHINE_ORT_SINGLE_THREAD
vibeos-dictate sets it to 1 unless it is set: Moonshine runs on one thread.
